<?xml version="1.0"?>
<robot xmlns:xacro="http://www.ros.org/wiki/xacro">

  <!--
    Intentionally empty. This used to hold Gazebo's native
    gz-sim-diff-drive-system / odometry-publisher / joint-state-publisher
    plugins, which directly commanded the wheel joints and published
    odom/tf/joint_states in parallel with gz_ros2_control's
    diff_drive_controller + joint_state_broadcaster. Running both at once
    meant two systems writing velocity commands to the same joints, and
    two publishers on /robot_2/odom, /robot_2/tf, and /robot_2/joint_states
    with mismatched frame ids (robot_2/base_link here vs. the unprefixed
    base_link/base_footprint everywhere else in the URDF).

    ros2_control (via ros2_control.xacro's GazeboSimSystem +
    my_controllers.yaml's diff_cont) is now the single source of truth for
    wheel commands, odom, and tf in sim, matching how the real robot
    (RealRobotSystem/Robot2System) works. Do not re-add these plugins
    alongside ros2_control.
  -->

</robot>